            <ArticleTitle>Oromandibular disorders and headache. A critical appraisal.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>929-45</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Oromandibular disorders are functional disorders and associated pains in the anatomic region of the temporomandibular joint. Their diagnosis and treatment are controversial because of the lack of conformity concerning these disorders among health care providers. This article provides a clear classification of these disorders and critically reviews their evaluation and treatment.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
